1
00:01:59,241 --> 00:02:03,891
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:03,955 --> 00:02:08,545
No living creature was hurt during the
production of this show.

3
00:02:30,953 --> 00:02:35,978
My Gonca, Gonca open your eyes.
Come on.

4
00:02:40,713 --> 00:02:45,923
Thank Allah you are with me in my
last breath.

5
00:02:46,141 --> 00:02:47,941
Sshhh.

6
00:02:47,986 --> 00:02:50,580
Don't say that, don't say it.

7
00:02:50,580 --> 00:02:53,511
Come on Gonca, we will return
to our tent.

8
00:02:53,511 --> 00:02:56,521
Open your eyes. Come on Gonca.

9
00:02:57,628 --> 00:03:00,068
Come on my rose, open your eyes.

10
00:03:49,256 --> 00:03:51,736
Gonca!
Gonca!

11
00:03:58,321 --> 00:03:59,981
Togay.

12
00:04:00,867 --> 00:04:02,447
Togay!

13
00:04:24,274 --> 00:04:27,174
Retreat!
Retreat!

14
00:04:45,655 --> 00:04:47,045
Hazal.

15
00:05:33,975 --> 00:05:36,645
Alps! Let's go!

16
00:05:40,375 --> 00:05:45,516
Gündüz! Where are you going, nephew?
Don't you see them retreating?

17
00:05:45,516 --> 00:05:50,483
Uncle! I won't stop chasing that dog!
Come on Alps!

18
00:05:50,483 --> 00:05:54,313
You take care of Abdulrahman Ghazi.
Let's go.

19
00:06:02,189 --> 00:06:06,489
- Gonca.
- Gonca.

20
00:06:08,199 --> 00:06:12,059
Look at me sister!
Gonca!

21
00:06:31,757 --> 00:06:35,587
Bamsı Bey. Bamsı Bey. Bamsı Bey.

22
00:06:42,038 --> 00:06:44,428
Abdulrahman Ghazi.

23
00:07:03,541 --> 00:07:05,441
Gonca.

24
00:07:05,947 --> 00:07:09,887
Mother. Mother.

25
00:07:13,818 --> 00:07:17,548
Wake up mother.
Get up.

26
00:07:17,734 --> 00:07:21,124
Wake up.
Get up.

27
00:07:23,806 --> 00:07:28,466
Alps! Take the woundeds to the tent.

28
00:07:31,531 --> 00:07:34,911
Bring the dead behind.

29
00:07:37,481 --> 00:07:40,741
Come on Gonca. Hold on.

30
00:07:43,121 --> 00:07:46,601
Hold on Gonca.
Let's go Boran

31
00:07:47,564 --> 00:07:51,014
Hold on Gonca, hold on my rose.

32
00:07:51,017 --> 00:07:53,017
Hold on.

33
00:07:58,621 --> 00:08:01,661
Hold on daughter.
Hold on daughter.

34
00:08:03,778 --> 00:08:07,198
Mother!
Mother!

35
00:08:18,038 --> 00:08:19,908
Stop there.

36
00:08:21,550 --> 00:08:23,770
Alps!

37
00:08:35,036 --> 00:08:39,686
Do you think you can dogmatise us just
because you gave us land, Osman Bey?

38
00:08:40,042 --> 00:08:44,822
Hatun, your stubborness drives both sides
to cliff.

39
00:08:45,804 --> 00:08:50,104
Both you and your father
are pushing my patience.

40
00:08:50,223 --> 00:08:52,431
Tell your Alps to fall back.

41
00:08:52,431 --> 00:08:57,201
Don't make me make a choice between my
respect for you and my Bey's command.

42
00:08:57,201 --> 00:09:00,581
You trust me, but how come you still
sell horses to my enemy?

43
00:09:04,351 --> 00:09:10,261
You promised trade before land. You told
us you wouldn't interfere.

44
00:09:11,344 --> 00:09:15,342
We trusted you. We accepted your
invitation.

45
00:09:15,342 --> 00:09:20,322
Now either you keep your promise,
or we go down together.

46
00:09:20,395 --> 00:09:27,285
Alps! Appropriate the horses before
I do something crazy.

47
00:09:31,710 --> 00:09:33,250
Bahadır!

48
00:10:14,360 --> 00:10:19,400
Since when does Kayı Bey waylay, Osman Bey?
This is banditry.

49
00:10:19,544 --> 00:10:24,914
I let you trade. I didn't let you
arm my enemy.

50
00:10:32,530 --> 00:10:37,150
Do your trade. Sell your sheep, sell your
goats, sell your milk.

51
00:10:37,338 --> 00:10:42,298
But do not sell horses.
Horses are Turks' weapon.

52
00:10:43,088 --> 00:10:48,458
You can't sell horses. You can't sell
stallion. You can't sell weapon.

53
00:10:49,390 --> 00:10:51,670
You can't sell arrow.

54
00:10:55,621 --> 00:11:01,521
Take your goods and go to Inegol.
Make your trade.

55
00:11:02,960 --> 00:11:10,110
I am taking these horses.
I'll give you double whatever Nicola did.

56
00:11:13,382 --> 00:11:18,152
From now on, this treason will end here.

57
00:11:18,960 --> 00:11:21,890
Search for treason in your tent,
Osman Bey.

58
00:11:23,880 --> 00:11:29,650
As long as that betrayer lives, we won't
unite. You should know that.

59
00:11:31,969 --> 00:11:33,729
Alps!

60
00:11:36,692 --> 00:11:38,322
Let's go.

61
00:11:44,616 --> 00:11:46,266
Alps!

62
00:12:48,510 --> 00:12:49,960
Come on!

63
00:12:57,292 --> 00:13:01,792
My Bamsı Bey, Abdulrahman Ghazi has
been martyred.

64
00:13:05,095 --> 00:13:09,925
I will find and kill that betrayer.

65
00:13:14,206 --> 00:13:16,576
I'll kill that betrayer.

66
00:13:20,302 --> 00:13:22,822
What betrayer are you talking about,
Bamsı Bey?

67
00:13:23,131 --> 00:13:28,681
The betrayer in the tent was potter Idris.
He is dead now.

68
00:13:28,760 --> 00:13:31,010
What betrayer are you talking about?

69
00:13:32,509 --> 00:13:37,449
Has treason ended, Dündar Bey?
Has treason ended?

70
00:13:38,874 --> 00:13:41,384
It is still in us!

71
00:13:42,659 --> 00:13:46,719
I will find and kill that betrayer,
Dündar Bey.

72
00:14:07,576 --> 00:14:09,826
We lost their tracks, my Bey.

73
00:14:16,434 --> 00:14:19,334
Let's go back.
Come on!

74
00:15:03,259 --> 00:15:09,249
Bamsı Bey, let us take Abdulrahman Ghazi
to the tent.

75
00:15:09,799 --> 00:15:11,349
Come on.

76
00:15:12,684 --> 00:15:14,404
Keep your hands off.

77
00:15:16,272 --> 00:15:19,132
Hands off, Dündar Bey.

78
00:15:20,590 --> 00:15:22,940
Keep your hands off.

79
00:16:41,842 --> 00:16:43,702
Alps!

80
00:16:45,973 --> 00:16:48,213
Alps!

81
00:16:50,997 --> 00:16:52,547
Alps...

82
00:16:54,739 --> 00:16:57,589
Have you seen what happened to us?

83
00:17:00,614 --> 00:17:02,914
Have you seen what happened to us?

84
00:17:06,475 --> 00:17:12,095
Abdulrahman Ghazi was martyred.

85
00:17:19,832 --> 00:17:22,102
Abdulrahman Ghazi...

86
00:17:23,777 --> 00:17:26,757
Our Abdulrahman Ghazi
was martyred, my Bey.

87
00:17:46,574 --> 00:17:48,834
Who did this?

88
00:17:51,770 --> 00:17:56,500
Bala is taking Gonca and the wounded Alps
to the tent.

89
00:17:56,610 --> 00:17:58,590
Who did this?

90
00:17:59,382 --> 00:18:01,662
Who did this?!

91
00:18:07,388 --> 00:18:10,438
It's Togay, my Bey.
It's Togay.

92
00:18:13,828 --> 00:18:15,788
Sons.

93
00:18:22,770 --> 00:18:27,750
Do you see, Alps?
Can you see what happened?

94
00:18:28,419 --> 00:18:30,779
Do you see it?

95
00:18:31,821 --> 00:18:36,731
Abdulrahman Ghazi has been martyred.

96
00:18:38,205 --> 00:18:41,045
Oi my Ghazi

97
00:18:42,862 --> 00:18:45,102
My dear fellow.

98
00:18:45,853 --> 00:18:50,243
Come on get up, Kayı's valiant.

99
00:18:51,557 --> 00:18:56,017
Come on, get up, get up and stand.

100
00:18:56,668 --> 00:19:00,098
Just like the previous battles.
Get up.

101
00:19:00,755 --> 00:19:03,395
Stand up. Stand up.

102
00:19:04,359 --> 00:19:08,819
Get on your dark horse...

103
00:19:09,731 --> 00:19:12,221
and go one war to another.

104
00:19:13,458 --> 00:19:19,278
Arrive to the mountains, hunt there.

105
00:19:21,107 --> 00:19:24,427
Come on my Ghazi, come on.

106
00:19:28,687 --> 00:19:33,127
My valiant alp.
My valiant Ghazi.

107
00:19:33,840 --> 00:19:38,030
We were going to be together.

108
00:19:39,776 --> 00:19:41,476
We were going to go together.

109
00:19:43,207 --> 00:19:47,727
You are a martyr now.

110
00:19:53,016 --> 00:19:55,026
Togay!

111
00:20:22,392 --> 00:20:28,232
Abdurrahman Ghazi, my dear fellow.
You are a martyr now.

112
00:20:29,291 --> 00:20:31,421
You are a martyr.

113
00:20:31,852 --> 00:20:36,552
Once you died once...

114
00:20:38,956 --> 00:20:44,556
This Bamsı died one thousand times.

115
00:20:46,678 --> 00:20:48,678
One thousand times.

116
00:20:58,563 --> 00:21:02,683
My Lord! Give this ghazi of
the ghazis....

117
00:21:03,496 --> 00:21:08,126
place in your heaven.

118
00:21:08,634 --> 00:21:12,504
Give this ghazi of the ghazis place
in your heaven.

119
00:21:30,288 --> 00:21:32,588
My Osman.

120
00:21:35,055 --> 00:21:37,975
Abdulrahman Ghazi deceased.

121
00:21:50,927 --> 00:21:53,947
He is a martyr now.

122
00:22:07,736 --> 00:22:13,716
Oi my Ghazi.
Go to Ucmag(heaven).

123
00:22:29,204 --> 00:22:30,584
Alps!

124
00:22:31,709 --> 00:22:38,089
Abdulrahman Ghazi lodged like a caravan...

125
00:22:39,903 --> 00:22:42,483
And now he moved, he is gone.

126
00:22:50,191 --> 00:22:54,701
He left me alone here.

127
00:23:12,258 --> 00:23:15,968
Abdulrahman Ghazi was a heirloom.

128
00:23:19,212 --> 00:23:20,652
Now...

129
00:23:24,652 --> 00:23:27,712
Now you have arrived at the rank of
shahada.

130
00:23:41,603 --> 00:23:42,973
Now...

131
00:23:47,930 --> 00:23:49,730
Now we have to...

132
00:23:52,844 --> 00:23:55,384
take revenge.

133
00:24:26,391 --> 00:24:28,481
Can I come in?

134
00:24:28,764 --> 00:24:30,124
Come.

135
00:24:35,132 --> 00:24:38,082
Have the caravan arrived in Inegol?

136
00:24:38,534 --> 00:24:41,834
Osman Bey waylaid and took the horses.

137
00:24:42,397 --> 00:24:45,077
Ahh Osman Bey ahh!

138
00:24:45,420 --> 00:24:48,270
If only you knew my intentions are good!

139
00:24:48,553 --> 00:24:52,023
If only you could reveal the betrayer
in your tent!

140
00:24:52,455 --> 00:24:57,565
At that time we would destroy that
infidel's castle together!

141
00:25:00,309 --> 00:25:03,279
But no.

142
00:25:03,312 --> 00:25:08,022
What are we going to do father?
Osman Bey doesn't know it. He is angry.

143
00:25:08,381 --> 00:25:12,351
He let us take goods to Inegol, but
appropriated the horses.

144
00:25:12,578 --> 00:25:15,428
It seems difficult to take the castle
down now.

145
00:25:20,149 --> 00:25:22,779
It's time I met Osman Bey.

146
00:25:23,597 --> 00:25:25,877
Let me go with you my father.

147
00:25:27,227 --> 00:25:29,997
- Get alps ready.
- As you command.

148
00:25:37,160 --> 00:25:42,590
Umur Bey sent what we wanted, but it's not
good that Osman appropriated the horses.

149
00:25:43,042 --> 00:25:45,702
Do you think I care about
the horses, Helen?

150
00:25:46,606 --> 00:25:53,566
I do not need horses to fight, I only need
two tents' alps to fall in each other.

151
00:26:00,291 --> 00:26:05,261
Osman's banditry must have made
Umur Bey furious.

152
00:26:05,801 --> 00:26:11,161
While they are messing with each other,
we will complete our things in Sogut.

153
00:26:11,941 --> 00:26:17,011
When Kalanoz joins, Helen,
it will be over.

154
00:26:25,120 --> 00:26:28,110
Sir, a Mongol wants to see you.

155
00:26:28,369 --> 00:26:31,699
- Who is he?
- He said he brought news from Togay.

156
00:26:31,769 --> 00:26:33,569
Let him in.

157
00:26:34,648 --> 00:26:35,918
Doors!

158
00:26:59,352 --> 00:27:05,422
The wedding was ruined, so was Osman's
dignity.

159
00:27:06,128 --> 00:27:07,718
Who are you?

160
00:27:10,002 --> 00:27:13,712
Geyhatu's Commander Camuha.

161
00:27:14,912 --> 00:27:16,462
Camuha.

162
00:27:17,350 --> 00:27:19,119
Where is Togay?

163
00:27:19,119 --> 00:27:21,639
Commander Togay is on his way to Konya.

164
00:27:22,803 --> 00:27:27,413
It was reported that some Lords didn't
pay their taxes to Seljuqs.

165
00:27:32,197 --> 00:27:39,117
Camuha, I do not talk politics with
people I don't know.

166
00:28:46,957 --> 00:28:49,177
Ah Abdulrahman Ghazi.

167
00:28:50,052 --> 00:28:55,402
You said shahada even in the wedding.

168
00:28:56,083 --> 00:28:58,233
Ah Abdulrahman Ghazi.

169
00:29:02,493 --> 00:29:04,973
My time has also come.

170
00:29:05,386 --> 00:29:11,526
From now on, I, too, want to be a martyr.

171
00:29:42,989 --> 00:29:44,379
My Bey!

172
00:29:45,489 --> 00:29:48,309
Why do you want to become a martyr?

173
00:29:54,469 --> 00:29:59,779
I'll see my prophet.
I'll see my prophet.

174
00:30:00,678 --> 00:30:03,758
Then, I'll see my brothers.

175
00:30:03,777 --> 00:30:07,307
I'll see Doğan, I'll see my Ertugrul Bey.

176
00:30:07,568 --> 00:30:09,828
Then I'll see my children.

177
00:30:11,181 --> 00:30:16,371
I'll see my Aybars, Aslıhan,
I'll see my Hafza.

178
00:30:20,853 --> 00:30:24,223
This is what it is, Cerkutay.

179
00:30:24,260 --> 00:30:28,310
Some come, some go.

180
00:30:30,576 --> 00:30:31,716
My Bey.

181
00:30:34,026 --> 00:30:36,046
In old times...

182
00:30:37,921 --> 00:30:39,881
When an important man died...

183
00:30:42,889 --> 00:30:45,999
people used to be sacrificed...

184
00:30:48,369 --> 00:30:50,879
to accompany his soul.

185
00:30:54,613 --> 00:31:00,023
If you die, I'll sacrifice
all the enemies.

186
00:31:05,431 --> 00:31:10,541
Cerkutay, we Muslims don't do that

187
00:31:10,628 --> 00:31:15,788
We donate to the poors so that...

188
00:31:15,868 --> 00:31:20,638
the good prayers shall accompany the
dead's soul.

189
00:31:26,927 --> 00:31:30,097
I only have my armor and sword.

190
00:31:32,952 --> 00:31:37,882
Nevermind, I'll sell them and feed
the poor.

191
00:31:38,419 --> 00:31:40,679
They will pray for you, my Bey.

192
00:31:41,533 --> 00:31:45,473
Oi Cerkutay, Oi Cerkutay.

193
00:31:45,473 --> 00:31:47,653
What am I going to do with you?

194
00:31:47,808 --> 00:31:53,628
Son, you have a huge heart.
What a huge heart you have!

195
00:31:54,006 --> 00:31:55,986
You don't need wealth.

196
00:32:08,296 --> 00:32:13,396
The face you see is Geyhatu's.

197
00:32:14,702 --> 00:32:20,222
Now listen to me in view of this fact.

198
00:32:22,080 --> 00:32:24,790
Osman wasn't in the wedding caravan.

199
00:32:26,146 --> 00:32:29,286
The lovers' nupital was wasted.

200
00:32:29,883 --> 00:32:33,423
Oldish Abdurrahman died.

201
00:32:34,252 --> 00:32:39,932
The heirlooms he was supported by
are dying one by one.

202
00:32:41,718 --> 00:32:46,328
Now it is Umur Bey's tent's turn.

203
00:32:54,992 --> 00:32:57,962
Togay didn't say that.

204
00:32:58,443 --> 00:33:01,783
What's the rush?

205
00:33:02,157 --> 00:33:05,637
Geyhatu commanded us to
finish this at once...

206
00:33:05,821 --> 00:33:11,531
and conquer Sogut, found a headquarters.

207
00:33:20,035 --> 00:33:21,655
Did you say Sogut?

208
00:33:35,275 --> 00:33:37,945
We have a lot to do.

209
00:33:38,829 --> 00:33:43,179
You and your soldiers must be tired.

210
00:33:44,351 --> 00:33:47,101
Now that you are the face of Geyhatu...

211
00:33:47,741 --> 00:33:51,161
then I want to host you well.

212
00:33:54,963 --> 00:33:56,563
Commander Mikis.

213
00:33:59,921 --> 00:34:03,631
Lead our guests to their rooms.

214
00:34:03,698 --> 00:34:06,788
Give a feast for them.

215
00:34:23,184 --> 00:34:27,594
This is no good, we were about to
corner Umur Bey.

216
00:34:28,085 --> 00:34:30,865
Togay is missing.
Nicola...

217
00:34:31,688 --> 00:34:37,548
if Mongols conquer Sogut, we won't
have the power anymore.

218
00:34:37,755 --> 00:34:40,845
- I won't let them.
- How?

219
00:34:40,847 --> 00:34:45,097
I will make Osman attack on Mongols
like Togay is here.

220
00:34:45,530 --> 00:34:50,495
When Togay comes back, he will neither be
able to found a headquarters in Sogut...

221
00:34:50,495 --> 00:34:53,795
nor attack Umur Bey.

222
00:34:55,302 --> 00:34:58,522
Smart move, that's what I like.

223
00:35:32,656 --> 00:35:34,576
What happened here?

224
00:35:34,686 --> 00:35:37,176
It smells bad news.

225
00:35:40,559 --> 00:35:43,429
This is dog Togay or Nicola's job!

226
00:36:00,813 --> 00:36:02,946
Apply this salve

227
00:36:02,946 --> 00:36:04,856
May it work out inshallah.

228
00:36:08,494 --> 00:36:10,024
My Gonca?

229
00:36:12,390 --> 00:36:14,420
Thank Allah.

230
00:36:15,534 --> 00:36:19,624
We stopped the bleeding.
You'll get better inshallah.

231
00:36:21,010 --> 00:36:23,060
Thank you my Bala.

232
00:36:27,510 --> 00:36:31,460
Having a wedding while in a war could
be like this at most.

233
00:36:32,320 --> 00:36:34,770
You'll have better days.

234
00:36:36,090 --> 00:36:37,750
Can I come in?

235
00:36:38,299 --> 00:36:39,879
Come.

236
00:36:52,922 --> 00:36:56,012
Boranalp, you take the watch.

237
00:37:07,553 --> 00:37:11,073
I told you we could fight and have
a wedding.

238
00:37:13,139 --> 00:37:18,349
But you didn't say that we'd do
both at the same time.

239
00:37:20,602 --> 00:37:22,502
The wedding is a pretext.

240
00:37:23,620 --> 00:37:27,990
The man and woman comes together,
guests have fun.

241
00:37:37,134 --> 00:37:44,554
However, when two lovers come together,
each day becomes a wedding day.

242
00:37:48,295 --> 00:37:50,485
Get rest.

243
00:37:51,221 --> 00:37:53,711
Vengenace is my job.

244
00:37:55,661 --> 00:37:58,761
Thank Allah our enemy is apparent.

245
00:37:59,924 --> 00:38:02,254
Once Osman Bey commands us...

246
00:38:03,409 --> 00:38:05,179
blood will drip out of my sword.

247
00:38:07,967 --> 00:38:15,767
I swear I will bury a Mongol for
each sigh you have.

248
00:38:39,093 --> 00:38:40,668
Bala Hatun.

249
00:38:40,668 --> 00:38:43,188
What happened?
Who attacked you?

250
00:38:44,167 --> 00:38:46,477
Who can it be?

251
00:38:49,824 --> 00:38:52,104
Who is our enemy?

252
00:38:57,009 --> 00:39:00,879
Togay and Nicola's soldiers who you tried
to sell horses came together...

253
00:39:01,474 --> 00:39:03,994
and raided our wedding caravan.

254
00:39:04,852 --> 00:39:08,942
Bala Hatun, it's not like how it seems.

255
00:39:13,939 --> 00:39:17,519
Where is Osman Bey?
I want to see him.

256
00:39:20,379 --> 00:39:23,133
They are burying martyr Abdurrahman Ghazi.

257
00:39:23,133 --> 00:39:25,573
Abdurrahman Ghazi ha?

258
00:39:28,052 --> 00:39:31,272
Yes, Abdurrahman Ghazi.

259
00:39:33,944 --> 00:39:37,484
Oh, Abdurrahman Ghazi, oh.

260
00:39:43,383 --> 00:39:47,213
My Bey, Osman Bey has arrived.
He is in his tent.

261
00:39:49,638 --> 00:39:53,758
I'll see Osman Bey, give him
my condolences.

262
00:39:58,123 --> 00:40:01,605
Alaca, if Hatuns need any help...

263
00:40:01,605 --> 00:40:03,035
Malhun Hatun.

264
00:40:04,170 --> 00:40:09,050
It's not necessary. We'll take care of
our own.

265
00:40:10,693 --> 00:40:14,473
We only need you to not work with
the betrayers.

266
00:40:26,040 --> 00:40:29,290
Why did you let her talk like that,
Malhun Hatun?

267
00:40:29,982 --> 00:40:34,202
Their pain is fresh. It's not
the right time.

268
00:40:52,797 --> 00:40:54,697
Can I come in Osman Bey?

269
00:40:59,305 --> 00:41:01,035
Come.

270
00:41:11,930 --> 00:41:14,220
My condolences, Osman Bey.

271
00:41:15,211 --> 00:41:17,981
I heard about Abdurrahman Ghazi.

272
00:41:21,793 --> 00:41:24,063
He was my Ghazi father's fellow.

273
00:41:26,895 --> 00:41:30,005
He lost his arm to protect our tent.

274
00:41:31,853 --> 00:41:37,133
Now he died for my alps.

275
00:41:40,228 --> 00:41:42,738
My condolences again, Osman Bey.

276
00:41:43,567 --> 00:41:45,277
I feel you.

277
00:41:55,119 --> 00:41:59,669
Togay raided the wedding caravan.

278
00:42:10,203 --> 00:42:13,223
He'll pay for this eventually, Osman Bey.

279
00:42:14,283 --> 00:42:17,523
What about you, Umur Bey?

280
00:42:19,433 --> 00:42:22,803
What am I supposed to pay for?

281
00:42:22,934 --> 00:42:27,084
Soldiers of Nicola who you made trade
were also there.

282
00:42:27,513 --> 00:42:31,803
They helped Togay.
Do you know that?

283
00:42:33,121 --> 00:42:36,983
I only made a trade agreement with
Nicola.

284
00:42:36,983 --> 00:42:41,893
Moreover, Nicola didn't recieve
the horses.

285
00:42:42,598 --> 00:42:48,610
I don't trust Nicola's friendship or
loyalty. I don't vouch for him!

286
00:42:48,610 --> 00:42:51,040
Nicola is my biggest enemy.

287
00:42:51,088 --> 00:42:54,468
What are you talking about?

288
00:42:56,426 --> 00:42:59,658
He attacked today, I will attack tomorrow.

289
00:42:59,658 --> 00:43:02,348
There will be a bloodshed.

290
00:43:03,753 --> 00:43:09,363
You are trying to make trades in this
bloodshed!

291
00:43:09,874 --> 00:43:16,644
Osman Bey, attacking a wedding caravan
is lowness, of course!

292
00:43:17,689 --> 00:43:23,329
But we are not the ones who are to
prevent that.

293
00:43:24,914 --> 00:43:29,814
The land is yours.
You have the responsibility.

294
00:43:30,406 --> 00:43:36,696
You are right. This is my land.
This is my responsibilty.

295
00:43:36,696 --> 00:43:39,756
Vengeance is mine!

296
00:43:39,827 --> 00:43:45,047
But, it's too late for Nicola.

297
00:43:47,192 --> 00:43:54,322
I will not show mercy if someone gets
between us, even my fellows.

298
00:44:09,529 --> 00:44:14,979
Who can put you off from taking
your rightous revenge?

299
00:44:16,242 --> 00:44:19,862
We are ready to help.

300
00:44:23,938 --> 00:44:26,358
I have spoken.

301
00:44:28,073 --> 00:44:30,983
Just get out of my way, that's enough.

302
00:44:53,448 --> 00:44:55,248
Get down.

303
00:44:58,636 --> 00:45:02,566
I brought news from Lord Nicola.
I want to see Osman Bey.

304
00:45:20,389 --> 00:45:22,039
Go.

305
00:45:33,159 --> 00:45:35,087
Can I come in, my Bey?

306
00:45:35,087 --> 00:45:36,657
Come.

307
00:45:42,536 --> 00:45:45,176
My Bey, Nicola sent a messenger.

308
00:45:45,868 --> 00:45:47,528
Take him in.

309
00:46:37,699 --> 00:46:40,179
The head infidel Nicola...

310
00:46:44,204 --> 00:46:47,164
reveals where Togay is hiding.

311
00:46:53,194 --> 00:46:57,504
He says he has nothing to do with
the raid...

312
00:47:00,588 --> 00:47:05,338
and he is not with Togay anymore.

313
00:47:08,632 --> 00:47:11,112
We can't trust him.

314
00:47:11,467 --> 00:47:14,007
This is a new game of Nicola's, Osman Bey.

315
00:47:15,029 --> 00:47:19,029
Did this guy just want to be our friend
out of nothing?

316
00:47:20,348 --> 00:47:22,678
I know this is a trap.

317
00:47:25,145 --> 00:47:27,345
But we'll go anyways.

318
00:47:28,075 --> 00:47:31,035
Where are we going to go, Osman Bey?
To a trap?

319
00:47:31,326 --> 00:47:34,546
We will, brother. We will.

320
00:47:34,794 --> 00:47:38,164
We will take precautions and go.

321
00:47:41,540 --> 00:47:44,420
Because we have no other option.

322
00:47:45,142 --> 00:47:49,052
I'll chase every chance that can give
me Togay.

323
00:47:55,113 --> 00:48:00,383
I don't think Nicola would set up such
an obvious trick.

324
00:48:01,005 --> 00:48:04,305
Maybe it's right that they fell in
each other with Togay.

325
00:48:06,074 --> 00:48:08,733
But we have to be sure
about it, Osman Bey.

326
00:48:08,733 --> 00:48:11,943
We'll see, brother, we'll see.

327
00:48:12,198 --> 00:48:15,148
But first, we have to go.

328
00:48:15,596 --> 00:48:18,032
Get alps ready.

329
00:48:18,032 --> 00:48:19,822
Command is yours, Osman Bey.

330
00:48:32,232 --> 00:48:36,352
This is Nicola's payment for our goods,
my Bey.

331
00:48:37,157 --> 00:48:40,237
Good job, Bahadır.
Eyvallah (thank you).

332
00:48:43,708 --> 00:48:45,758
You can get out now.

333
00:48:58,415 --> 00:49:04,905
We will continue making trades with Nicola
to infiltrate in Inegol Castle.

334
00:49:12,013 --> 00:49:14,163
What about Osman Bey?

335
00:49:14,780 --> 00:49:18,130
He sees us as a betrayer, just like
all the Kayı tents.

336
00:49:19,052 --> 00:49:22,552
This bothers me too.

337
00:49:24,687 --> 00:49:28,897
We were held responsible for the
raid...

338
00:49:30,571 --> 00:49:32,481
to the wedding caravan.

339
00:49:34,757 --> 00:49:39,247
Why are you not telling our real intention
to sell Nicola the horses, my Bey?

340
00:49:43,179 --> 00:49:49,119
Even though we are seen as a betrayer
in front of Osman Bey and his tent...

341
00:49:50,097 --> 00:49:53,207
we can't reveal our game.

342
00:49:56,301 --> 00:50:01,071
As long as we can't reveal that betrayer
in Kayı...

343
00:50:01,593 --> 00:50:05,183
We can't explain our intentions.

344
00:50:05,315 --> 00:50:09,315
Then, Nikola will find out our goal.

345
00:50:09,315 --> 00:50:15,745
The owner of the thumb ring is still in
the tribe and Osman Bey is accusing us.

346
00:50:19,537 --> 00:50:26,327
Don't worry. The time is coming
for that traitor.

347
00:50:47,562 --> 00:50:51,562
They are getting ready
to march, my bey.

348
00:50:52,323 --> 00:50:56,733
They are many. It looks like they
are going for a raid.

349
00:50:56,733 --> 00:50:58,673
But...

350
00:50:59,632 --> 00:51:03,632
...we couldn't see Togay, my bey.

351
00:51:05,241 --> 00:51:11,151
If his warriors are here, he must
be around.

352
00:51:12,111 --> 00:51:17,011
Brother, I will finish Togay off,
and you will take the warriors.

353
00:51:17,011 --> 00:51:21,571
Don't worry. None will survive.

354
00:51:26,120 --> 00:51:29,570
Come on.

355
00:51:51,558 --> 00:51:53,878
Alps!

356
00:51:59,120 --> 00:52:03,120
For Abdurrahman Ghazi!

357
00:53:46,235 --> 00:53:48,665
A trap!

358
00:56:10,025 --> 00:56:14,025
Where are you Togay?

359
00:56:16,007 --> 00:56:23,777
When Togay returns, I'll give
your head to him, Osman!

360
00:57:10,224 --> 00:57:14,224
Togay, where are you?

361
00:57:23,722 --> 00:57:29,252
Alps! We are returning.
Come on!

362
00:58:52,206 --> 00:58:56,206
-Brother.
-Nikola's news were true.

363
00:58:56,983 --> 00:59:01,563
But the commander of these
pagan mongols...

364
00:59:01,563 --> 00:59:05,563
...Togay isn't here.
Where might he be, Osman Bey?

365
00:59:05,939 --> 00:59:11,059
When Togay returns, I will
give your head to him!

366
00:59:12,319 --> 00:59:17,019
The mongol that ran away said
'When Togay returns'.

367
00:59:17,129 --> 00:59:21,129
It's apparent that he isn't around.

368
00:59:21,458 --> 00:59:29,178
But Nikola's news show that they
don't have a true alliance.

369
00:59:32,755 --> 00:59:36,755
What's on your mind, my bey?

370
00:59:44,614 --> 00:59:48,614
We'll break that tie.

371
00:59:49,371 --> 00:59:55,941
They'll take each others' heads.

372
01:00:30,336 --> 01:00:37,266
How did Osman find us so easily?

373
01:00:38,325 --> 01:00:45,005
According to the information Commander
Togay gave, there is only one way to find out.

374
01:00:46,369 --> 01:00:49,869
We are going to Söğüt.

375
01:01:48,208 --> 01:01:53,008
Camuha...you?
What are you doing here?

376
01:01:53,008 --> 01:01:58,848
Petros, did you tell Togay's
location?

377
01:01:59,664 --> 01:02:02,594
-No...
-Who then?

378
01:02:02,594 --> 01:02:06,794
-I don't know.
-Dündar!

379
01:02:11,042 --> 01:02:15,042
Only Dündar can know that.

380
01:02:19,233 --> 01:02:23,233
If you have the shadow of
treason on you...

381
01:02:23,873 --> 01:02:27,873
...Togay's sword will behead you.

382
01:02:30,149 --> 01:02:33,789
Why would we betray...

383
01:02:34,381 --> 01:02:37,701
...both our target is Osman.

384
01:02:41,215 --> 01:02:45,215
Our path is stony.

385
01:02:45,467 --> 01:02:52,597
If you think it's hard, your death
won't be easy either.

386
01:02:55,919 --> 01:02:59,919
You'll write a letter for Dündar.

387
01:03:02,237 --> 01:03:09,007
When Togay finds out that it was
Nikola, they'll alliance will break.

388
01:03:09,597 --> 01:03:15,732
If Nikola sold Togay out,
he must have a reason.

389
01:03:17,148 --> 01:03:22,828
We'll use this opportunity. We won't
stop, we'll pursue.

390
01:03:23,326 --> 01:03:31,846
We'll run through these lands and
tear Togay apart.

391
01:03:32,940 --> 01:03:38,820
-Inshallah.
-Togay deserved what's coming.

392
01:03:38,820 --> 01:03:44,780
But, Osman Bey, we need to
take care of Nikola first.

393
01:03:46,283 --> 01:03:56,223
Bamsı Bey is right. If we take care of
Nikola first, Togay will be an easy prey.

394
01:03:57,930 --> 01:04:02,610
We have the strength to beat
them both, thank Allah.

395
01:04:02,849 --> 01:04:07,609
We have the strength, thank Allah.
And we have the passion.

396
01:04:08,192 --> 01:04:13,832
The conquest of İnegöl will be easier
with the support of the beys.

397
01:04:17,788 --> 01:04:21,788
-May I enter, my bey?
-Come.

398
01:04:27,531 --> 01:04:32,431
-Brother.
-I congratulate your efforts, brother.

399
01:04:33,026 --> 01:04:37,026
Thank you, brother.
Welcome.

400
01:04:38,064 --> 01:04:43,914
-But you are early.
-I have important news, brother.

401
01:04:44,308 --> 01:04:46,098
Tell me.

402
01:04:46,098 --> 01:04:50,778
I got information from a merchant
from Constantinople.

403
01:04:51,599 --> 01:04:56,309
Brother of Kalamos that you killed
is coming to İnegöl with great numbers.

404
01:04:58,232 --> 01:05:02,232
They'll reach the castle tomorrow
evening.

405
01:05:02,866 --> 01:05:08,926
-Then, we don't have time.
-We should act at once, Bamsı Bey.

406
01:05:09,697 --> 01:05:15,317
It seems that Nikola is
worried about his life.

407
01:05:16,299 --> 01:05:23,169
He knows that İnegöl will fall.
Beys, this news is important.

408
01:05:23,329 --> 01:05:29,899
Before İnegöl's conquest gets harder,
we should be on the battlefield.

409
01:05:30,090 --> 01:05:35,320
You have the sword of jihad, Osman Bey.
Just say the word.

410
01:05:35,320 --> 01:05:40,090
We'll be there at once.

411
01:05:41,234 --> 01:05:45,234
Thank you, Bamsı Bey.
Thank you.

412
01:05:46,309 --> 01:05:49,999
-Thank you, brother.
-Thank you, brother.

413
01:05:49,999 --> 01:05:54,309
We'll stop them before reaching
the castle.

414
01:05:54,464 --> 01:05:59,574
Inform the tribe beys. They should
come with a few alps.

415
01:05:59,574 --> 01:06:04,094
If not with numbers, why do you
want them to come, Osman Bey?

416
01:06:04,094 --> 01:06:09,574
They'll get a taste of the jihad.

417
01:06:11,697 --> 01:06:18,807
They should get used to the
idea of unity.

418
01:06:20,419 --> 01:06:26,419
Brother, I want the beys and
the alps ready at the dawn.

419
01:06:26,419 --> 01:06:32,079
Don't worry. We'll bring them
all to the battlefield.

420
01:06:32,824 --> 01:06:39,354
Thank you. The conquest of İnegöl
depends on cutting this support.

421
01:06:39,354 --> 01:06:44,314
We'll hit the heathens
as hard as we can.

422
01:06:59,269 --> 01:07:06,939
Sir, do you think that Osman trusted
us and attacked Camuha?

423
01:07:09,029 --> 01:07:14,029
A wolf pursues the prey even
if it's dangerous.

424
01:07:14,029 --> 01:07:20,049
Even if he didn't see Togay there,
he must've killed Camuha and his men.

425
01:07:21,330 --> 01:07:27,300
Who knows? Maybe they killed
each other already.

426
01:07:27,300 --> 01:07:30,201
What if Camuha is alive?

427
01:07:30,201 --> 01:07:35,101
Togay will find out that you
were behind this.

428
01:07:35,417 --> 01:07:40,257
According to what Camuha said, Mongols
will use the Seljuks...

429
01:07:40,257 --> 01:07:45,670
...to collect taxes through
the new lord.

430
01:07:49,910 --> 01:07:53,910
Mongols...
Mongols...

431
01:07:54,177 --> 01:08:00,657
The only thing they care about is taxes.
They don't care about the Seljuks or Byzantines.

432
01:08:00,797 --> 01:08:07,057
Kalanoz will be here tomorrow.
I'll have not only Söğüt...

433
01:08:08,966 --> 01:08:12,966
...but the honor of killing Togay.

434
01:08:13,942 --> 01:08:20,602
Kalanoz must be running here to get
the revenge of his brother.

435
01:08:22,258 --> 01:08:27,388
Those who chase revenge are
rebellious.

436
01:08:27,388 --> 01:08:33,978
I will control Kalanoz's anger for
my victory.

437
01:08:58,648 --> 01:09:02,648
I was awaiting you, Dündar Bey.

438
01:09:12,025 --> 01:09:16,025
Won't you tell me what happened?

439
01:09:16,025 --> 01:09:22,255
They were silent for a long time, woman.
Now, they are calling me.

440
01:09:22,532 --> 01:09:24,252
Süleyman?

441
01:09:24,252 --> 01:09:30,032
Both Osman and the Pope's dogs
think that they use me.

442
01:09:30,233 --> 01:09:34,563
But I used them.

443
01:09:35,216 --> 01:09:40,616
This took too long, Dündar Bey.

444
01:09:40,616 --> 01:09:44,236
This isn't good.

445
01:09:44,236 --> 01:09:48,776
We should cut it off, woman.

446
01:09:48,776 --> 01:09:53,440
I should behead the one in between
me and the throne.

447
01:09:55,051 --> 01:10:00,161
I know, you are afraid.
And you are right.

448
01:10:00,161 --> 01:10:06,731
The doomsday is close.
So, I'll get Togay to their hands.

449
01:10:06,891 --> 01:10:10,891
Don't forget what happened
with Balgay.

450
01:10:13,349 --> 01:10:17,849
I have nothing else to lose
but my head, woman.

451
01:10:20,358 --> 01:10:25,188
I want you to go to Kastamonu.

452
01:10:25,188 --> 01:10:29,188
I shouldn't look behind
at the doomsday.

453
01:10:32,657 --> 01:10:38,397
If we'll die, we'll die together,
Dündar Bey.

454
01:10:39,298 --> 01:10:43,988
Together and upright.

455
01:10:55,159 --> 01:10:59,159
How will you find Togay?

456
01:11:00,597 --> 01:11:05,387
After Osman's attack, he will find me.

457
01:11:05,387 --> 01:11:10,837
I will blow my last strike to Osman
with Togay.

458
01:11:11,151 --> 01:11:14,011
Inshallah.

459
01:12:00,096 --> 01:12:02,986
Bala.

460
01:12:08,548 --> 01:12:14,578
What happened to Gonca Hatun
makes you sad.

461
01:12:18,546 --> 01:12:22,036
Her wound is healing, my bey.

462
01:12:22,418 --> 01:12:26,418
But what happened there...

463
01:12:32,321 --> 01:12:38,541
Don't keep it in you.
Share it with me, Bala.

464
01:12:38,802 --> 01:12:42,802
I'm afraid to give you trouble, my bey.

465
01:12:48,282 --> 01:12:50,872
Come.

466
01:12:52,820 --> 01:12:55,610
Come.

467
01:13:07,499 --> 01:13:11,499
Words words can only heal me.

468
01:13:14,615 --> 01:13:17,065
Osman.

469
01:13:18,615 --> 01:13:22,615
Gonca and Boran Alp hardly
found any time to marry.

470
01:13:24,145 --> 01:13:29,295
And they were attacked at
that wedding.

471
01:13:30,275 --> 01:13:34,275
When we think such things happen...

472
01:13:34,275 --> 01:13:40,165
...we'll await attacks
at every moment.

473
01:13:41,589 --> 01:13:46,799
Osman Bey, this endless war...

474
01:13:47,022 --> 01:13:51,022
...if it stops us from doing
weddings...

475
01:13:51,022 --> 01:13:55,022
...celebrations, funerals...

476
01:13:59,969 --> 01:14:06,269
...we can't expand, reproduce...

477
01:14:06,269 --> 01:14:08,679
...build families.

478
01:14:12,360 --> 01:14:16,360
You spoke like a Khatun.

479
01:14:21,520 --> 01:14:24,860
You are right.

480
01:14:25,099 --> 01:14:28,339
You are right, Bala.

481
01:14:29,523 --> 01:14:36,703
But this is the fate of the people...

482
01:14:37,258 --> 01:14:42,028
...who aims to break chains...

483
01:14:43,136 --> 01:14:46,286
...and build a state for
the oppressed.

484
01:14:47,180 --> 01:14:55,510
My mission is to save my tribe
from this fire.

485
01:15:00,142 --> 01:15:05,862
We'll have good days, Bala.
We'll have good days.

486
01:15:06,213 --> 01:15:10,213
Our children will grow up
in peace.

487
01:15:11,432 --> 01:15:17,322
We'll have weddings and
holidays.

488
01:15:17,624 --> 01:15:24,524
Our elders, sisters won't
be have to go to wars.

489
01:15:27,982 --> 01:15:31,982
We'll have an army.

490
01:15:32,446 --> 01:15:36,446
We'll have a state.

491
01:15:40,028 --> 01:15:46,008
We will.
We will, Bala.

492
01:15:46,449 --> 01:15:51,139
Inshallah, my bey.
Inshallah.

493
01:15:57,392 --> 01:16:03,112
-If you allow me.
-Of course.

494
01:16:16,440 --> 01:16:20,440
We will.

495
01:16:29,010 --> 01:16:30,460
Dumur Bey's Tribe

496
01:16:30,460 --> 01:16:32,970
What will we do now, my bey?

497
01:16:32,970 --> 01:16:36,970
-May I enter, my bey?
-Come, my daughter.

498
01:16:42,250 --> 01:16:47,170
-You summoned me, my bey.
-Osman Bey...

499
01:16:48,076 --> 01:16:53,646
Osman Bey still doesn't recognize me.

500
01:16:57,770 --> 01:17:04,480
He neglects the blood I spilled for my
country, my sons that I sacrificed...

501
01:17:04,480 --> 01:17:08,480
-What happened, my bey?
-He doesn't even want to hear...

502
01:17:08,480 --> 01:17:13,000
...how I stood straight against
the armies of Geyhatu.

503
01:17:17,932 --> 01:17:25,562
Now, it's time he finds out.

504
01:17:28,032 --> 01:17:35,752
He wants me to shepherd my people
like his lambs.

505
01:17:40,145 --> 01:17:44,225
It's time to show our fangs.

506
01:17:44,225 --> 01:17:48,895
-What are you saying, father?
-Osman Bey...

507
01:17:49,804 --> 01:17:56,514
...is preparing for jihad.
He invited all the tribes except us.

508
01:17:57,678 --> 01:18:03,458
He's trying to ruin our reputation
in front of the other tribes.

509
01:18:04,240 --> 01:18:09,490
-That's what it's all about.
-We can't let that happen, father.

510
01:18:11,666 --> 01:18:15,666
Of course, we won't.

511
01:18:15,666 --> 01:18:20,686
Malhun, go to Osman Bey
with Bahadır.

512
01:18:21,629 --> 01:18:26,929
Let them know who we are.

513
01:18:31,982 --> 01:18:38,462
Osman Bey, you can't harm my honor.

514
01:20:05,887 --> 01:20:12,397
-Who are you?
-Togay's shadow, Camuha.

515
01:20:12,397 --> 01:20:15,077
Speak.

516
01:20:18,456 --> 01:20:24,836
Osman raided you, so you want
to know who sold you out, huh?

517
01:20:24,836 --> 01:20:28,526
Speak.

518
01:20:28,526 --> 01:20:33,826
You should kill Osman, not me.

519
01:20:34,174 --> 01:20:37,094
Speak!

520
01:20:37,094 --> 01:20:41,094
It's Nikola who sold you out.

521
01:20:42,368 --> 01:20:45,838
Togay must've forgot to feed Nikola.

522
01:20:45,838 --> 01:20:53,248
Nikola wants us to face the Kayıs.

523
01:20:53,757 --> 01:20:56,867
Why is he doing that?

524
01:20:56,867 --> 01:21:02,887
It seems like they choose Umur bey
as a friend.

525
01:21:03,746 --> 01:21:09,856
If Togay had informed me, I would
tell him everything.

526
01:21:09,856 --> 01:21:15,996
If Togay had trusted me, you wouldn't
lose all your warriors.

527
01:21:19,642 --> 01:21:23,642
Wait for a word from Togay.

528
01:22:14,442 --> 01:22:21,322
-May Allah bless your efforts, Osman Bey.
-Thank you, Bala. Thank you.

529
01:22:22,282 --> 01:22:27,016
Osman Bey, alps are waiting for you
with Savcı Bey.

530
01:22:27,016 --> 01:22:32,046
-Thank you, brother.
-Turkmen Beys are also waiting.

531
01:22:32,046 --> 01:22:36,686
Come on. Let us be on our way.

532
01:23:33,824 --> 01:23:40,724
We heard that you are going to a jihad,
Osman Bey. My father wants us to join.

533
01:23:40,724 --> 01:23:44,724
We have enough alps, Malhun Hatun.

534
01:23:45,064 --> 01:23:50,094
Now, we need to be on our way at once.

535
01:23:50,797 --> 01:23:54,357
Are you denying us the jihad, Osman Bey?

536
01:23:54,357 --> 01:23:58,357
You should stand in front of those
who are going to a jihad.

537
01:23:59,684 --> 01:24:03,684
What are your intentions, Osman Bey?

538
01:24:04,223 --> 01:24:08,833
You are stopping our trade,
you are stopping our jihad...

539
01:24:09,773 --> 01:24:13,773
...did you invite us to these borderlands
to sit like elders?

540
01:24:13,989 --> 01:24:18,909
I invited you to support me,
not to defy me.

541
01:24:19,489 --> 01:24:24,589
I invited you to be my ally,
not to be my enemy.

542
01:24:24,589 --> 01:24:29,049
Should I focus on you or the
enemy on the battlefield?

543
01:24:31,601 --> 01:24:36,281
Now, get out of my way.

544
01:25:34,775 --> 01:25:40,585
Malhun Hatun. Come and drink
something with me.

545
01:25:40,585 --> 01:25:44,585
Let us talk woman to a woman.

546
01:25:46,793 --> 01:25:50,123
Come on!

547
01:26:40,894 --> 01:26:44,084
Hold!

548
01:26:48,249 --> 01:26:55,109
Commander, follow me with the archers.
Scout the way ahead. Inform the army.

549
01:26:58,999 --> 01:27:01,459
Forward.

550
01:27:17,315 --> 01:27:24,805
We have news from the scouts.
The Byzantines will come through Karakuş Hill.

551
01:27:29,552 --> 01:27:34,662
Commander Kalamoz is coming with
his vanguards...

552
01:27:34,662 --> 01:27:40,064
...ahead of his army.

553
01:27:40,521 --> 01:27:47,121
My bey, is a realitive of Lord Kalamoz
that you killed before?

554
01:27:47,395 --> 01:27:51,635
It's his brother.

555
01:27:51,635 --> 01:27:55,635
He seeks revenge.

556
01:27:55,635 --> 01:28:02,075
He'll burn in his own fire.
We'll fight for Abdurrahman Ghazi.

557
01:28:06,079 --> 01:28:10,109
Thank you.
Thank you.

558
01:28:10,109 --> 01:28:16,069
My beys, we'll attack them
at the Valley of Kördüğüm.

559
01:28:16,717 --> 01:28:22,547
This is the battlefield.

560
01:28:26,310 --> 01:28:31,560
Brother Gündüz, you will attack
from these hills.

561
01:28:32,341 --> 01:28:37,341
Brother Savcı, you will go through
this road.

562
01:28:37,341 --> 01:28:41,341
Don't worry, Osman Bey.

563
01:28:42,553 --> 01:28:47,823
Bamsı Bey, you will lead the archers.

564
01:28:47,823 --> 01:28:53,823
Thank you, Osman Bey.
We'll pierce them. Don't worry.

565
01:28:55,530 --> 01:28:59,530
Thank you.

566
01:28:59,824 --> 01:29:05,004
And I will face Kalamoz.

567
01:29:05,356 --> 01:29:11,886
The army that the emperor sent with
Kalamoz is coming to take our homes.

568
01:29:13,434 --> 01:29:20,414
It's our duty to stop them from
reaching the castle.

569
01:29:24,093 --> 01:29:28,093
-May Allah help us.
-Amin!

570
01:29:28,093 --> 01:29:32,093
May Allah bless our efforts.

571
01:29:54,749 --> 01:29:57,169
Come on.

572
01:29:59,092 --> 01:30:04,102
Is that so? He has enough alps, huh?

573
01:30:06,668 --> 01:30:13,498
I guessed it. He is trying to
harm our reputation...

574
01:30:14,568 --> 01:30:19,888
...and make us look like traitors in
front of the other beys.

575
01:30:20,035 --> 01:30:26,795
Don't worry, my father. Everyone knows
how loyal you are to Turkish traditions.

576
01:30:29,818 --> 01:30:33,818
But...

577
01:30:33,818 --> 01:30:37,818
...are you sure that you don't want to
speak about your trade with Nikola?

578
01:30:37,818 --> 01:30:41,228
Of course, I am.

579
01:30:41,228 --> 01:30:45,228
Osman Bey won't know this.
He won't, so that...

580
01:30:46,106 --> 01:30:51,336
...Nikola won't know my real
intentions.

581
01:30:53,235 --> 01:30:58,635
While he is busy with Kalamoz and
Togay...

582
01:30:59,605 --> 01:31:05,625
...we will conquer İnegöl Castle.

583
01:31:09,249 --> 01:31:13,759
Bahadır! Come here.

584
01:31:17,564 --> 01:31:23,704
How are the beys who rallied
to Osman's help?

585
01:31:24,321 --> 01:31:30,691
They need help, my bey.
They are all in bad conditions.

586
01:31:30,691 --> 01:31:36,853
They are far from doing the trade they
hoped but they are helping Osman.

587
01:31:46,005 --> 01:31:51,885
Everyone was sad because of the
death of Dervish Zülfikar.

588
01:31:51,885 --> 01:31:55,246
And they were attacked on
their way back, my sheik.

589
01:31:57,095 --> 01:32:01,825
The bride is wounded on her chest,
and the groom is in his heart.

590
01:32:04,637 --> 01:32:08,637
The path of love is difficult,
Dervish Akça.

591
01:32:09,995 --> 01:32:15,955
The people of Söğüt are affected.
Shopkeepers are worried.

592
01:32:19,479 --> 01:32:25,579
Are the intentions of the shopkeepers
and the dervishes are different, Kumral Abdal?

593
01:32:28,769 --> 01:32:32,769
They both buy and sell, my sheik.

594
01:32:35,072 --> 01:32:39,792
I understand the shopkeepers but what
do dervishes buy and sell?

595
01:32:39,792 --> 01:32:44,482
They sell their desires and buy
the approval of Allah.

596
01:32:50,491 --> 01:32:55,861
Do you see, Akça?
Dervishes trade too.

597
01:32:56,402 --> 01:33:02,782
And both the dervishes and the shopkeepers
seek peace.

598
01:33:03,695 --> 01:33:07,695
May I enter, my sheik?

599
01:33:08,399 --> 01:33:11,769
Peace...

600
01:33:11,956 --> 01:33:15,186
Come, my daughter.

601
01:33:17,524 --> 01:33:22,614
If the peace has come,
we should leave, my sheik.

602
01:33:37,693 --> 01:33:41,693
Bala, my heart.

603
01:33:42,628 --> 01:33:47,388
My eyes, come, sit.

604
01:33:57,750 --> 01:34:00,780
Father.

605
01:34:06,633 --> 01:34:11,833
Allah gave the opportunity and
I ran to you.

606
01:34:11,833 --> 01:34:16,223
I'm thankful for that mighty
and good Allah.

607
01:34:17,873 --> 01:34:21,573
Tell me, what are you doing?

608
01:34:21,573 --> 01:34:27,113
I'm busy with the tribe's works.
Osman Bey is on jihad.

609
01:34:28,977 --> 01:34:32,977
He wants to punish
the attackers.

610
01:34:34,133 --> 01:34:38,133
Ghazis also do trade, my daughter.

611
01:34:38,516 --> 01:34:44,126
They buy and sell lives,
with Allah's approval.

612
01:34:46,048 --> 01:34:52,088
They become ghazis by taking and
martyrs by giving.

613
01:34:56,324 --> 01:35:03,434
Bala, tell me.
What is the real matter?

614
01:35:04,024 --> 01:35:09,544
My sheik, Osman Bey's
only trouble isn't the heathens.

615
01:35:09,544 --> 01:35:14,704
The people he thinks to be friends,
make troubles and they complain.

616
01:35:15,556 --> 01:35:19,556
Umur Bey is a valiant Turkmen bey...

617
01:35:19,556 --> 01:35:24,196
...who has swung his sword against
the pagan Mongols for all his life.

618
01:35:26,126 --> 01:35:31,808
Osman Bey is a commander of
ghazis...

619
01:35:31,808 --> 01:35:37,708
...who try to proselytize Allah's religion
with his bare sword on these lands.

620
01:35:39,278 --> 01:35:43,278
But Umur Bey and his daughter
Malhun Hatun.

621
01:35:52,149 --> 01:35:59,509
Muslims are worried about their future
in between the Mongols and the Rums.

622
01:36:02,876 --> 01:36:10,676
They can't bear a fight between
beys.

623
01:36:16,525 --> 01:36:20,525
This can't go on.

624
01:36:40,484 --> 01:36:43,084
Hold!

625
01:36:43,935 --> 01:36:50,365
Archers will hold this hill.
We are close to Turkish lands.

626
01:36:50,365 --> 01:36:55,715
Osman ambushed the last army.
We'll be cautious.

627
01:36:55,715 --> 01:36:58,715
Archers!

628
01:37:51,138 --> 01:37:54,378
Kalamoz!

629
01:37:54,378 --> 01:37:59,878
You came for revenge!
I'm here! Come on!

630
01:37:59,878 --> 01:38:03,184
Osman! God damn it!

631
01:38:15,596 --> 01:38:19,166
Archers, shoot!

632
01:38:43,865 --> 01:38:47,325
Archers, shoot!

633
01:39:06,033 --> 01:39:08,643
Shoot!

634
01:39:18,702 --> 01:39:21,332
Alps!

635
01:39:25,190 --> 01:39:28,320
Shoot!

636
01:39:42,960 --> 01:39:45,380
Protect Osman Bey!

637
01:39:48,733 --> 01:39:52,733
Alps! For Allah!

638
01:41:36,724 --> 01:41:37,924
Kalanoz.

639
01:42:24,673 --> 01:42:26,703
If you don't talk...

640
01:42:48,250 --> 01:42:49,630
Brother.

641
01:42:49,970 --> 01:42:50,900
Bamsı Bey.

642
01:42:50,975 --> 01:42:55,495
- Some of the soldiers ran away, my Bey.
- They can't run away, brother.

643
01:42:56,333 --> 01:42:58,313
Are we going to follow them?

644
01:42:58,696 --> 01:43:01,896
Mongols will kill them before they
arrive at the castle.

645
01:43:09,236 --> 01:43:14,096
Spirits want blood!

646
01:43:14,514 --> 01:43:17,674
For our dead soldiers...

647
01:43:18,253 --> 01:43:20,723
for Togay...

648
01:43:21,341 --> 01:43:27,061
don't feel pity! Kill them all!

649
01:43:27,121 --> 01:43:29,801
We won't let them run away!

650
01:43:37,439 --> 01:43:39,269
Mongols, huh?

651
01:43:43,712 --> 01:43:47,182
They knew Nikola told me where they hid.

652
01:43:49,508 --> 01:43:51,848
We killed many of their soldiers.

653
01:43:52,059 --> 01:43:57,239
They want to take revenge on Nikola.

654
01:43:57,809 --> 01:44:00,519
Didn't we kill the soldiers?

655
01:44:00,732 --> 01:44:06,462
That's why they sent my brother the news
via a merchant from Constantin.

656
01:44:08,614 --> 01:44:13,374
We didn't set a trap for Kalanoz.
Mongols did.

657
01:44:13,577 --> 01:44:17,737
Nice.
Let them kill each other.

658
01:44:18,129 --> 01:44:22,309
While the jackals fight, the lion
comes out.

659
01:44:23,174 --> 01:44:27,374
They both will serve us.

660
01:44:30,155 --> 01:44:34,545
Until I rip their lungs off.

661
01:44:44,142 --> 01:44:47,602
Give the Beys their prizes.

662
01:44:47,797 --> 01:44:50,747
They will get what they deserve.

663
01:44:50,946 --> 01:44:53,076
Thank you.

664
01:44:53,841 --> 01:44:57,761
Kalanoz's soldiers are wretched.

665
01:44:57,883 --> 01:45:00,693
He is an intelligent commander
even he has been trapped.

666
01:45:00,791 --> 01:45:03,421
He took his soldiers and
went to the forest.

667
01:45:03,643 --> 01:45:07,853
He saved himself even though most of
his soldiers are dead.

668
01:45:09,780 --> 01:45:11,270
What about...

669
01:45:11,669 --> 01:45:16,229
the Beys who came to support Osman Bey?

670
01:45:16,360 --> 01:45:19,100
Osman Bey is an intelligent
soldier, my Bey.

671
01:45:19,213 --> 01:45:22,303
They came with their Alps.

672
01:45:24,039 --> 01:45:25,749
He says...

673
01:45:26,190 --> 01:45:30,530
he can win a victory without us.

674
01:45:33,215 --> 01:45:34,305
However...

675
01:45:34,938 --> 01:45:39,598
he doesn't want to deprive us of
the war's good deed.

676
01:45:41,505 --> 01:45:43,785
Their tent is in a difficult
situation, my Bey.

677
01:45:43,802 --> 01:45:48,652
From now on, each Alp that Osman Bey wants
will put them in a difficult situation.

678
01:45:59,154 --> 01:46:01,674
What are you thinking, my Bey?

679
01:46:02,404 --> 01:46:06,784
I want to invite all of the Beys
to my tent.

680
01:46:08,298 --> 01:46:10,698
Send news to them.

681
01:46:11,591 --> 01:46:13,661
Your command, my Bey.

682
01:46:17,760 --> 01:46:21,760
Osman Bey deprives us of the honor
of the war.

683
01:46:22,599 --> 01:46:28,239
However, we will stand by the Beys who are
also in the war.

684
01:46:28,897 --> 01:46:33,727
We will save them from Osman Bey.

685
01:46:35,902 --> 01:46:38,942
We will show them they are not alone.

686
01:46:46,089 --> 01:46:50,089
Kalanoz lost most of his soldiers.

687
01:46:50,557 --> 01:46:55,467
This means that İnegöl won't get
a help.

688
01:46:58,015 --> 01:46:59,915
Nikola and Togay being enemies...

689
01:47:00,877 --> 01:47:04,657
makes our work easier and possible.

690
01:47:06,111 --> 01:47:09,991
Turkmen Beys kept their promises.

691
01:47:11,101 --> 01:47:13,891
Osman Bey, as you know...

692
01:47:14,024 --> 01:47:17,814
war is war, prize is a prize.

693
01:47:20,067 --> 01:47:23,797
Turkmen Beys wait for it now.

694
01:47:24,115 --> 01:47:26,865
It is a religious duty to be in the war...

695
01:47:27,215 --> 01:47:30,665
however, we need to relieve their wounds.

696
01:47:31,453 --> 01:47:36,043
We should support them
and make them happy.

697
01:47:39,383 --> 01:47:41,833
Beys are right, Osman Bey.

698
01:47:41,930 --> 01:47:45,430
All of them have a responsibility
for their own tent.

699
01:47:47,340 --> 01:47:50,300
I know about their conditions.

700
01:47:51,002 --> 01:47:55,192
From the day I drive union politics...

701
01:47:55,553 --> 01:48:00,133
I know what they need and what they lack.

702
01:48:04,281 --> 01:48:07,131
I know their financial
conditions are bad.

703
01:48:07,284 --> 01:48:13,264
However, they don't want
to expose themselves.

704
01:48:16,631 --> 01:48:19,231
- Uncle.
- Yes, my Bey.

705
01:48:19,906 --> 01:48:23,906
Send news to merchants and craftsmen.

706
01:48:24,497 --> 01:48:28,267
Make up the needs of everyone...

707
01:48:28,662 --> 01:48:31,882
who came to the war or not.

708
01:48:32,538 --> 01:48:35,288
They should see me for the count.

709
01:48:35,461 --> 01:48:39,141
They will get more if they help.

710
01:48:40,337 --> 01:48:44,337
Send news to Beys, too. They should
come to my tent.

711
01:48:44,689 --> 01:48:48,689
They should see that I didn't
invite them just for the war.

712
01:48:49,990 --> 01:48:53,090
We will help them if they need anything.

713
01:48:53,263 --> 01:48:55,743
We will relieve their wounds.

714
01:48:56,608 --> 01:49:00,608
They will see our union's power
and benefits.

715
01:49:00,934 --> 01:49:04,674
So that, when we say there is a war...

716
01:49:04,978 --> 01:49:08,708
they should help us with love and
eagerness.

717
01:49:09,588 --> 01:49:13,188
Thank you.

718
01:49:15,685 --> 01:49:16,725
Thank you.

719
01:49:21,158 --> 01:49:23,588
Thank you, Osman Bey.

720
01:49:41,299 --> 01:49:43,349
My Bala.

721
01:49:45,183 --> 01:49:49,743
I heard you talk, my Bey.
Are there many martyrs?

722
01:49:53,057 --> 01:49:56,287
The victory is of Muslim Turks, my Bala.

723
01:49:58,719 --> 01:50:01,359
Our martyrs are in heaven.

724
01:50:01,606 --> 01:50:04,386
Of course, they are, my Osman.

725
01:50:05,975 --> 01:50:08,925
However, I want to help the ones rest.

726
01:50:20,833 --> 01:50:23,893
I love your beautiful heart.

727
01:50:24,409 --> 01:50:26,179
Hatun of Kayı.

728
01:50:26,715 --> 01:50:32,285
Who will relieve the wounds of children
and Hatuns, other than you?

729
01:51:04,877 --> 01:51:07,497
I have been serving you for years.

730
01:51:08,221 --> 01:51:10,991
I've seen your childhood.

731
01:51:11,459 --> 01:51:13,989
The times that you were a little girl.

732
01:51:15,876 --> 01:51:19,446
Your martyr brothers and
your mother loved you.

733
01:51:25,300 --> 01:51:27,960
My brothers are martyrs.

734
01:51:29,417 --> 01:51:32,757
Now I'm responsible for my tent.

735
01:51:33,162 --> 01:51:34,142
You've changed.

736
01:52:00,154 --> 01:52:03,694
My hands are callused because
of the swords.

737
01:52:05,671 --> 01:52:07,181
And my heart.

738
01:52:16,149 --> 01:52:17,869
Alaca Hatun.

739
01:52:20,199 --> 01:52:24,659
- Am I arrogant?
- If you're asking this, no.

740
01:52:28,503 --> 01:52:31,793
Am I being unfair...

741
01:52:33,196 --> 01:52:35,776
to a man who struggles for our good?

742
01:52:36,152 --> 01:52:38,502
Who are you talking about?

743
01:52:40,351 --> 01:52:43,491
Osman Bey, Bey of Kayı.

744
01:52:45,399 --> 01:52:48,459
We want him to find the traitor.

745
01:52:49,668 --> 01:52:53,028
We pressure a man...

746
01:52:53,792 --> 01:52:57,792
who have got into a war with
both Rums and Mongols...

747
01:52:58,498 --> 01:53:00,988
and who tries his best for his tent.

748
01:53:01,913 --> 01:53:05,913
That's because we don't want
any problem, Malhun Hatun.

749
01:53:21,354 --> 01:53:26,214
- Who are you, Hatun?
- Malhun Hatun, daughter of Umur Bey.

750
01:53:28,248 --> 01:53:29,908
Daughter of Umur Bey?

751
01:53:30,471 --> 01:53:34,471
We're coming here.
Our fate is up to you.

752
01:53:34,594 --> 01:53:37,644
However, we are crowded.

753
01:53:37,723 --> 01:53:39,733
10.000 people will come.

754
01:53:39,805 --> 01:53:42,965
Can you handle it?

755
01:53:49,511 --> 01:53:52,091
Look for the traitor
in your own tent, Osman Bey.

756
01:53:52,328 --> 01:53:56,788
We won't be united as long as
the traitor is alive.

757
01:53:56,849 --> 01:53:58,809
Keep that in mind.

758
01:53:59,137 --> 01:54:00,957
You save your tent well, Osman Bey!

759
01:54:01,170 --> 01:54:05,630
We trusted in your words.
Is that your promise?

760
01:54:05,691 --> 01:54:10,721
Don't say things that you don't want to.
You're angry.

761
01:54:11,011 --> 01:54:14,091
My anger isn't related to that, Osman Bey.

762
01:54:14,136 --> 01:54:18,136
What confuses my mind is that I
have trusted you.

763
01:54:18,278 --> 01:54:20,178
I should've not trusted you.

764
01:54:20,744 --> 01:54:25,724
I know who to suspect
as long as you don't bring him.

765
01:54:27,097 --> 01:54:30,637
Don't you trust my word, Malhun Hatun?

766
01:54:31,605 --> 01:54:34,195
My father, who trusted you...

767
01:54:34,467 --> 01:54:36,747
is wounded now.

768
01:54:37,575 --> 01:54:41,775
I know you're angry.
However, we have the same enemy.

769
01:54:42,807 --> 01:54:45,987
They want to set us against
each other, obviously.

770
01:54:46,256 --> 01:54:48,886
You're in trouble, Osman Bey.

771
01:54:49,063 --> 01:54:51,653
How will you handle it?

772
01:54:52,052 --> 01:54:53,882
We want him to find the traitor.

773
01:54:54,788 --> 01:54:58,058
However, we hide stuff from him.

774
01:55:02,022 --> 01:55:05,452
I think we're being
unfair to a valiant Bey.

775
01:55:18,823 --> 01:55:20,903
What kind of hell is this, Nikola?

776
01:55:21,044 --> 01:55:23,507
How come İnegöl is like that?

777
01:55:23,567 --> 01:55:29,077
- Do you understand me now, Kalanoz?
- Turks attacked me and my army.

778
01:55:29,425 --> 01:55:32,365
And Mongols killed my
soldiers who ran away.

779
01:55:32,430 --> 01:55:34,570
I know everything.

780
01:55:34,835 --> 01:55:39,015
How could you make Turks and
Mongols friends, Nikola?

781
01:55:40,731 --> 01:55:43,601
What you have to learn first
on these lands is...

782
01:55:43,717 --> 01:55:47,527
that no one will be friends, Kalanoz.

783
01:55:48,600 --> 01:55:55,480
We can't guess who will destroy who.

784
01:55:55,522 --> 01:55:59,002
I'm a soldier, Nikola!
I'm not a politician.

785
01:55:59,060 --> 01:56:03,650
I just want you to show
me the right target.

786
01:56:04,142 --> 01:56:07,682
Let me be sure who is
my friend or foe.

787
01:56:15,159 --> 01:56:19,159
I will show you how to take Söğüt.

788
01:56:19,639 --> 01:56:24,109
And you will take your brother's revenge.

789
01:57:05,611 --> 01:57:07,061
My Alps.

790
01:57:15,583 --> 01:57:16,943
do you know...

791
01:57:19,332 --> 01:57:21,362
why I hit you?

792
01:57:21,802 --> 01:57:23,402
They killed the lord.

793
01:57:25,404 --> 01:57:26,474
We...

794
01:57:36,433 --> 01:57:39,403
You could've taken measures
on the road, right?

795
01:57:42,441 --> 01:57:45,861
You could've protected the lord...

796
01:57:46,559 --> 01:57:50,149
with your shields, right?

797
01:57:57,000 --> 01:58:00,230
You could've done better, right?

798
01:58:00,383 --> 01:58:03,723
You're right, my Bey.
It won't happen again.

799
01:58:16,840 --> 01:58:19,680
Everyone makes mistakes.

800
01:58:21,026 --> 01:58:22,146
However...

801
01:58:25,510 --> 01:58:28,670
not again.

802
01:58:39,066 --> 01:58:40,996
My Alps.

803
01:58:43,130 --> 01:58:44,440
My valiants.

804
01:58:46,578 --> 01:58:48,058
My brothers.

805
01:59:00,979 --> 01:59:02,709
Brother.

806
01:59:05,161 --> 01:59:07,261
Don't worry.

807
01:59:07,728 --> 01:59:11,728
We'll take revenge on Togay.

808
01:59:12,456 --> 01:59:16,456
Yes, my Bey.
I know.

809
01:59:18,682 --> 01:59:20,942
However, I have a request.

810
01:59:22,151 --> 01:59:23,621
Tell me.

811
01:59:24,081 --> 01:59:28,951
When we have him, I want to kill him.

812
01:59:47,804 --> 01:59:49,074
My Bey.

813
01:59:49,146 --> 01:59:53,496
We did what you said. We let all the Beys
know. However...

814
01:59:53,684 --> 01:59:56,124
- What?
- Umur Bey.

815
01:59:56,247 --> 01:59:58,377
- He sent news to the Beys.
- So?

816
01:59:58,520 --> 02:00:02,520
The Beys will obey him and participate
in the meeting.

817
02:00:08,915 --> 02:00:11,195
Get the horses ready.

818
02:00:14,509 --> 02:00:16,739
Let's see...

819
02:00:17,449 --> 02:00:20,949
- what Umur Bey wants to do.
- Yes, my Bey.

820
02:00:21,217 --> 02:00:22,967
Alps, come on!

821
02:00:37,405 --> 02:00:41,315
Send my regards to Osman Bey and Umur Bey.

822
02:00:41,423 --> 02:00:43,403
They are both my guests.

823
02:00:43,554 --> 02:00:48,904
However, don't tell
Osman Bey that Umur Bey is coming and...

824
02:00:49,125 --> 02:00:54,125
don't tell Umur Bey that
Osman Bey is coming.

825
02:00:54,426 --> 02:00:57,036
Your command, my Sheikh.
As you command...

826
02:00:57,181 --> 02:01:01,181
we will bring them here without
knowing each other come.

827
02:01:11,261 --> 02:01:14,671
Let's end the separation already.

828
02:01:16,802 --> 02:01:20,802
They should unite, my Sheikh.

829
02:01:21,430 --> 02:01:25,430
So that they can reach what they want.

830
02:01:30,842 --> 02:01:32,502
Umur Bey's tent

831
02:01:32,960 --> 02:01:37,430
We know that there is always a
war in those lands...

832
02:01:38,718 --> 02:01:41,438
and there are always martyrs.

833
02:01:41,905 --> 02:01:48,035
Those martyrs are our martyrs. Ghazis are
our ghazis.

834
02:01:48,258 --> 02:01:53,238
It's our responsibility to
support their families.

835
02:02:16,095 --> 02:02:18,915
What are these golds?

836
02:02:19,228 --> 02:02:22,158
They are
what Ghazi and martyr families deserve.

837
02:02:22,269 --> 02:02:27,809
Even if Osman Bey doesn't give me and
my tent the honor of war...

838
02:02:27,990 --> 02:02:31,990
he can't prevent me from
supporting my brothers.

839
02:02:35,677 --> 02:02:39,677
My brothers, why do you doubt?

840
02:02:39,760 --> 02:02:41,140
It's what you deserve.

841
02:02:58,117 --> 02:03:03,237
Umur Bey, Osman has a right to have an
attitude against you.

842
02:03:06,618 --> 02:03:11,518
It's not okay
to trade with Nikola, Umur Bey.

843
02:03:13,755 --> 02:03:15,395
My brothers...

844
02:03:17,661 --> 02:03:20,561
Osman Bey misunderstood me.

845
02:03:20,697 --> 02:03:25,507
And you misunderstood me.

846
02:03:25,546 --> 02:03:29,266
I want you to know that...

847
02:03:29,376 --> 02:03:36,136
Umur Bey, son of Kızıl Bey,
has never been a traitor!

848
02:03:38,595 --> 02:03:42,685
My brothers, your tents have needs.

849
02:03:42,756 --> 02:03:47,336
How will you meet your needs without
trading?

850
02:03:47,636 --> 02:03:52,656
We have to trade to live on
in these lands.

851
02:03:52,843 --> 02:03:57,143
- Even Osman Bey has to trade.
- Tell me, Umur Bey.

852
02:03:59,319 --> 02:04:02,209
What does Osman Bey have to do?

853
02:04:11,482 --> 02:04:14,062
You came in without my
permission, Osman Bey.

854
02:04:15,237 --> 02:04:20,057
And you ask me questions.

855
02:04:25,900 --> 02:04:28,270
Answer me.

856
02:04:28,719 --> 02:04:31,519
I'm sure you have one.

857
02:04:44,774 --> 02:04:46,544
Tell me, then.

858
02:04:49,934 --> 02:04:55,954
Shouldn't be Beys helping each other in
difficult situations?

859
02:04:56,796 --> 02:05:00,796
Or do you consider this to be too much?

860
02:05:02,783 --> 02:05:05,463
I have invited them to the war.

861
02:05:06,258 --> 02:05:09,948
I will look after Ghazi's rights.

862
02:05:14,861 --> 02:05:20,631
Is Kayı Tent incapable of helping
their brothers?

863
02:05:21,754 --> 02:05:25,664
No, what kind
of words are they, Osman Bey?

864
02:05:25,687 --> 02:05:28,247
Right words!

865
02:05:30,424 --> 02:05:34,814
The words of
Osman Bey, son of Ertuğrul Ghazi!

866
02:06:47,607 --> 02:06:49,447
Father.

867
02:06:50,808 --> 02:06:54,198
Osman Bey did it again.

868
02:06:54,454 --> 02:06:57,584
He will see us as his enemies now.

869
02:06:59,173 --> 02:07:01,863
- Can I come in, my Bey?
- Come in.

870
02:07:06,768 --> 02:07:08,148
My Bey.

871
02:07:10,413 --> 02:07:12,923
From Sheikh Edebali.

872
02:07:28,057 --> 02:07:33,577
You deceived me. You let Togay
go over me.

873
02:07:34,192 --> 02:07:37,152
You should be happy
that you're alive, Dündar Bey.

874
02:07:39,663 --> 02:07:43,663
As you don't tell us Osman's intention...

875
02:07:44,181 --> 02:07:46,021
you don't stand by us.

876
02:07:46,262 --> 02:07:51,502
I'm sick of your betrayals
and plays, Süleyman.

877
02:07:52,279 --> 02:07:56,049
I want to live peacefully in my lands
and take what is mine.

878
02:07:56,123 --> 02:08:02,353
I have done what you say until today.
Now, it's your turn.

879
02:08:03,966 --> 02:08:06,866
Wow.

880
02:08:07,323 --> 02:08:12,923
So, Dündar Bey doesn't trust us anymore.

881
02:08:17,326 --> 02:08:19,946
Osman will die.

882
02:08:20,108 --> 02:08:25,328
You will be with me or you
will die with me.

883
02:08:28,832 --> 02:08:30,442
Then...

884
02:08:32,027 --> 02:08:36,027
let's talk and clear up the
problem, Dündar Bey.

885
02:08:36,329 --> 02:08:39,789
Who starts up in anger
sits down with a loss, brother.

886
02:08:44,599 --> 02:08:48,279
Tell us.
What do you want to do?

887
02:08:54,836 --> 02:08:58,196
My Bey. The
families of martyrs are waiting for you.

888
02:09:14,349 --> 02:09:16,529
Wait for my news.

889
02:09:16,905 --> 02:09:22,175
Not Nikola, not Togay.
We will do it three of us.

890
02:09:23,062 --> 02:09:26,692
Wait for my news.

891
02:09:37,396 --> 02:09:40,616
Will we trust him?

892
02:09:43,980 --> 02:09:47,880
We will act like it...

893
02:09:48,429 --> 02:09:50,839
until the day I kill him.

894
02:09:59,557 --> 02:10:06,917
Welcome, Osman Bey.

895
02:10:32,326 --> 02:10:34,386
Welcome, Osman Bey.

896
02:11:52,779 --> 02:11:57,769
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim. (In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful)

897
02:11:59,087 --> 02:12:03,617
- Salam Alaikum.
- Alaikum Salam, Osman Bey.

898
02:12:04,571 --> 02:12:07,581
Come.
It's an honor.

899
02:12:09,219 --> 02:12:11,639
Not at all, my Sheikh.

900
02:12:13,788 --> 02:12:17,788
You summoned me.
I came here quickly.

901
02:12:20,122 --> 02:12:24,682
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim. (In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful)

902
02:12:28,104 --> 02:12:32,204
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim. (In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful)

903
02:12:33,102 --> 02:12:37,102
May Allah rest our martyrs in peace.

904
02:12:38,747 --> 02:12:43,417
May Allah grant you what you want.

905
02:12:43,773 --> 02:12:47,033
Amin, my Sheikh.

906
02:12:48,621 --> 02:12:54,941
We have talked that the Islam community
is in separation.

907
02:12:56,235 --> 02:13:00,235
And we know what Muslims...

908
02:13:00,915 --> 02:13:04,235
are going through.

909
02:13:06,369 --> 02:13:12,959
Now, I know that Turkmen
Beys are separated.

910
02:13:15,533 --> 02:13:17,043
My Sheikh.

911
02:13:53,375 --> 02:13:59,175
- Salam Alaikum, my Sheikh.
- Alaikum Salam, Umur Bey.

912
02:14:01,123 --> 02:14:03,093
Alaikum Salam.

913
02:14:04,566 --> 02:14:08,146
Welcome, it's an honor.

914
02:14:08,550 --> 02:14:13,040
- It's an honor for me, my Sheikh.
- Come.

915
02:14:32,781 --> 02:14:38,131
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim. (In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful)

916
02:14:59,354 --> 02:15:04,154
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim. (In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful)

917
02:15:06,699 --> 02:15:11,259
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim. (In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful)

918
02:15:35,644 --> 02:15:39,854
If Turkmen Beys stood against Mongols...

919
02:15:40,469 --> 02:15:44,469
instead of standing against each other...

920
02:15:44,910 --> 02:15:47,940
would you migrate to Bithynia, Umur Bey?

921
02:15:48,244 --> 02:15:54,304
Who can devastate Turks
other than Turks, my Sheikh?

922
02:15:55,566 --> 02:16:00,646
That's why we invited our Beys.

923
02:16:00,750 --> 02:16:02,860
Our property...

924
02:16:03,916 --> 02:16:07,296
isn't at the center of Turk land.

925
02:16:08,836 --> 02:16:11,196
We are on the Byzantine border.

926
02:16:12,662 --> 02:16:14,482
What we take and...

927
02:16:15,391 --> 02:16:19,641
what we give is with Byzantine.

928
02:16:23,070 --> 02:16:27,690
The Turk's enemy is obvious.

929
02:16:29,649 --> 02:16:30,909
It is...

930
02:16:33,290 --> 02:16:34,720
Byzantine.

931
02:16:37,882 --> 02:16:42,482
They ally if needed.

932
02:16:43,865 --> 02:16:50,305
Mongols attack us when
we arrive the lands.

933
02:16:53,275 --> 02:16:54,885
My Beys.

934
02:16:55,769 --> 02:16:57,649
I see that...

935
02:16:59,107 --> 02:17:05,327
you think the same about Turk's aim
and freedom.

936
02:17:08,842 --> 02:17:12,842
Then, we should disappoint the ones...

937
02:17:12,842 --> 02:17:16,842
who want to harm us.

938
02:17:18,176 --> 02:17:23,956
The people believe that on Osman
Bey's property...

939
02:17:25,152 --> 02:17:29,712
Turkmen tents are peaceful and together.

940
02:17:30,132 --> 02:17:31,802
They are happy.

941
02:17:33,326 --> 02:17:36,796
The enemies should know
that the Turkmen tents...

942
02:17:36,971 --> 02:17:42,211
support Osman Bey.

943
02:17:45,661 --> 02:17:47,971
They should be afraid.

944
02:17:48,571 --> 02:17:50,081
Thank you.

945
02:17:50,996 --> 02:17:53,576
You're right, my Sheikh.

946
02:17:53,823 --> 02:17:55,543
However...

947
02:17:56,111 --> 02:17:59,551
Osman Bey...

948
02:17:59,781 --> 02:18:02,041
may Allah save us...

949
02:18:02,437 --> 02:18:06,737
Osman Bey sees us as traitors.

950
02:18:08,754 --> 02:18:12,734
We have told him that the traitor is...

951
02:18:13,574 --> 02:18:18,174
closer to him than us.

952
02:18:19,338 --> 02:18:21,408
- My Sheikh.
- Umur Bey...

953
02:18:24,412 --> 02:18:27,562
You are in the presence of our Sheikh.

954
02:18:33,004 --> 02:18:34,614
Tell us clearly.

955
02:18:36,829 --> 02:18:40,199
Who is the traitor closer to me
than you are?

956
02:18:41,840 --> 02:18:45,400
As you imply that you know something...

957
02:18:45,941 --> 02:18:49,941
then tell him and Osman Bey won't...

958
02:18:50,332 --> 02:18:55,562
suspect you again.

959
02:19:13,893 --> 02:19:17,463
The owner of this thumb ring... (thumb ring used
to draw the bow in the ottoman empire.)

960
02:19:17,520 --> 02:19:20,860
is the same person as the person
who shot the potter.

961
02:19:23,169 --> 02:19:25,039
The engraving on it...

962
02:19:26,234 --> 02:19:32,354
shows that it is someone
close to you, Osman Bey.

963
02:19:43,063 --> 02:19:45,003
My Sheikh.

964
02:20:27,088 --> 02:20:29,918
Uncle Dündar.

965
02:20:30,555 --> 02:20:34,555
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com